Z||000013||frontal lobe||09-13-2001||02:34 PM||||There are plenty of people on this planet that would love to take "MY PORTION" of it away by force, but the U.S. has decided to strengthen itself enough not to let that happen.  Canada has not decided to do that.  It has decided that it's friendly neighbor to the south is doing enough to protect "YOUR PORTION".  You are welcome.<P>I don't like the talk about use of nuclear weapons, either.  Completely not necessary to accomplish what needs to be accomplished.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tonker||09-13-2001||02:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by deceler8:<BR><B>My point is that terrorists have committed an action that until Tuesday was considered unthinkable and perhaps impossible.<P>These folks know the horror of death and destruction...sadly we've forgotten that lesson. But the terrorists have also forgotten the lessons of Hiroshima and Nagasaki. <P>Those that fail to learn from history are doomed to repeat it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you want to retaliate that's one thing. I would start with a demand that the Taliban trun over Bin-Laden and all his people. If they refuse start targeting ammo depots, power plants, government inrastructure with airstrikes and cruise missiles. If they still don't turn him over, send in the troops. Then   you have to make an example of this guy, whether you execute him, put him in jail, or cover him in honey and leave him for the ants is of no concern to me. Just make sure it's good.<P>Nukes should at no point enter the equation. Even at the tactical level, they are dirty weapons. They are weapons of terror.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroBUZZ||09-13-2001||02:38 PM||||Those individuals /organizations/ governments responsible should be identified and punished.  However lots of people in Afghanistan are NOT involved and it is not so very long ago that the Russians learned that it not so easy to subdue.<P>It's time for sober thought and planning, it seems to me that the US military thought they could carpet bomb N Vietnam.<P>I hate to think that 50 terrorists can cause WW III and the end of civilization.<P>Gary||||reg||8
Z||000016||GT Bastard||09-13-2001||02:41 PM||||STAY AWAY FROM NUCLEAR WEAPONS!!!  The last thing we need is a nuclear war.  Do you have any idea what the after-effects of nuclear war are?  Don't think for a second that these countries don't have nukes themselves...  I'm tired of the mentality of some people around here.  Those responsible need to die, not entire countries.||||reg||1
Z||000017||frontal lobe||09-13-2001||02:44 PM||||I don't care that nuclear weapons are weapons of terror.  Big deal.  Conventional weapons should be weapons of terror, too.  They should face terror.  That is all they respond to.  Not reason, morals, kindness, compassion, etc.<P>The point is that they are DIRTY as you said.  Why contaminate the environment for others instead of just going after who you really want with the conventional weapons.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Tonker||09-13-2001||02:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>There are plenty of people on this planet that would love to take "MY PORTION" of it away by force, but the U.S. has decided to strengthen itself enough not to let that happen.  Canada has not decided to do that.  It has decided that it's friendly neighbor to the south is doing enough to protect "YOUR PORTION".  You are welcome.<P>I don't like the talk about use of nuclear weapons, either.  Completely not necessary to accomplish what needs to be accomplished.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The problem with nukes is that you say, sure you might destroy my country, but I'll take the whole world with me. That includes the part of the world held by your enemies and allies alike. If no other country had nukes would you need them? Nope. The US has the conventional forces needed to defend itself from foreign attack. The only reason that you need nukes now is for deterrence.<P>If anyone invades Canada and your idea of saving us is with nukes, do me a favour... Let us go. Do I agree with the state of Canada's military? No. We have a more pathetic military than Iraq. Do I agree with with the state of Canada's nuclear forces? Yes. We don't want them, we don't need them, we're never going to use them. That's as it should be. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||fieronv||09-13-2001||03:00 PM||||Carpet bombing is not the answer to Bin Laden. He has hidden himself in caves and bunkers that the US built to survive Russian carpet bombing during the Afghani war with Russia. Atomic bombs either tactical or strategic is not the best way either. <BR>The US military has non nuclear weapon that are horrific enough to put fear into these people with out damaging the planet for decades. One weapon is a fuel air explosive that suck the oxygen from the area and the concussion will "jelly" the bones in your body. <BR>Unfortunately the only way that we will be able to get the people who did this is to send ground troops in and GET THEM. It will mean that we will lose more lives to these bastards but so be it. We have to teach these people that you can not do this and get away. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2_WEB_1.jpg">  <BR>85GT (twoloud)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||AkursedX||09-13-2001||03:08 PM||||Nuclear weapons are totally out of the question, in ANY case.  You just don't drop a nuke of any size and expect that it will just destroy intended area and that is all.  Eventually the air currents that circle this planet spreads out the radiation throughout the entire planet including our own country, giving a number of us nice, slow, cancerous deaths.  <P>Also if you use nukes, the will be a number of countries who support us now will not be too happy about the use of nuclear weapons, which could possibly blossom into more enemies for the United States.  <P>As for this idea of "destroying all terrorism"  by blowing up the entire Middle East, that will NOT get rid of terroism.  Yeah, you might destroy the people who hate us now, but that destruction will create more hatred towards the US from different groups.  <P>This whole idea of an eye for and eye is just rediculous.  We go into the Middle East and detroy everything and take innocent lives, what does that prove??  Does it prove we are the greatest country because we can kill the most people??  Well eventually, there will be someone who will be greater than us, and destroy us, that is inevitable.  Throughout history, no great empire has lasted forever, and nor will we, change is inevitable, whether it be tomorrow, or a hundred years from now.<P>There is no quick-fix solution to this, and to think that there is, is ignorance.  People want action now because this attack stirred up alot of emotion.  But people do alot of stupid things when they are filled with emotion.  Which is why America needs to calm down, take a look at the entire picture, and then react.  And no, I am not saying America should sit back and take this, we should act, just in a proper manner.  What that should be?  I don't know, but I am hoping the government will make a proper choice.<P>But the use of nukes, and or the taking of innocent lives as retribution, I feel is totally uncalled for.  But unfortuantely, I feel as if I'm a minority for feeling like this.  Oh well, we'll see what happens. <P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Sootah||09-13-2001||03:12 PM||||Frankly, I hope they hit us again. Now before you freak on me, call me a rag-headed, unpatriotic bastard, hear me out. I just heard the news about the sustained attack we are planning on terrorism. I merely don't think that at this point that the buerocracy is willing to take the steps neccisary to wipe this crap out. They are going to have to hit us again, then we will be ready. Enough of the tree-hugging pants-wetting crybabys will have been hurt enough to cry for war themselves. There is not a peacefull resolution to all of this. We are going to have to hit them at home, and we are going to have to hit them hard.<P>I don't think that we should use nukes, of any size. Enough countries have them now that it is entierly possible that they could throw a few of them back at us. I just think that a barrage of cruise missiles would do the trick. Then Afghanistan would turn over Bin Laden, Saddam would hopefully be dead, or at least devistated enough to not dare to try anything again.<P>Hit them, hit them all, and hit them hard.<P>Thank you.<P>-<B>Sootah</B><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">     <BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I> <BR><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter<P>EDIT: Damned typos<p>[This message has been edited by Sootah (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Formula88||09-13-2001||03:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B>The use of Nuclear weapons (or any other bio/chem) is [b]not</B> an acceptable solution whether they be tactical or strategic. I will not have you people destroy my fücking planet with those weapons! [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So, what about the nukes we used in Iraq during Desert Storm?  Small tactical nukes.  Not the big ones like Hiroshima or what most people think of when they think "nuke" but nuclear weapons, nontheless.  <P>Grow up and face reality.  A nuclear arsenal is there for a reason.  As a deterrant, and, if necessary, as a means of destruction.  I'm not advocating the use of nukes, or "glassing" a country.  I'm simply stating that to say, because they are nukes we shouldn't use them, is simplistic.<P>I hope it's not necessary to bomb a country back into the stone age, but if that's the course of action deemed necessary... so be it.||||reg||4
Z||000023||frontal lobe||09-13-2001||03:27 PM||||I didn't know we used any nuclear weapons in desert storm.  Did we?||||reg||1
