Z||000037||Taijiguy||09-13-2001||08:14 PM||||Mach10: You are correct, typo on my part, it was kilotons, vs megatons. They were 10-20 kilotons. The payload of the C-3 missiles was around 200 kilotons per warhead, with the capability of carrying multiple warheads on each missle, 16 missiles on board. (I could tell you how many warheads, but then I have to kill you)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>The most interesting thing about them is, they are what's called "one point safe" meaning you could fire a weapon right into the heart of the warhead, hitting the explosive, and the result would be nothing more than a detonation of the explosive, with no real effect on the raw materials, or any kind of nuclear reaction.<BR>I say we make ourselves some glass parking lots. Hell, we gotta do SOMETHING with those old missles...||||reg||4
